{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 15:53:29.915767", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### **Network Health Overview**\\nThe network appears to have connectivity issues between certain hosts and infrastructure devices. While some devices are able to communicate successfully, others are unable to establish connections, leading to incomplete reachability across the network.\\n\\n#### **Findings**\\n1. **Reachability Status**\\n   - **Successful Communication**:\\n     - The DNS server successfully communicates with the DHCP server (`10.200.0.8`) with no packet loss and an average RTT of 1.095 ms.\\n     - The Load Balancer (`10.200.0.7`) successfully communicates with the DHCP server with no packet loss and an average RTT of 1.483 ms.\\n     - All web servers (`web_server_0`, `web_server_1`, `web_server_2`, `web_server_3`) successfully communicate with the DHCP server with no packet loss and average RTTs ranging from 1.01 ms to 1.552 ms.\\n\\n   - **Failed Communication**:\\n     - Hosts (`host_1_1_1_1` and `host_2_1_1_1`) are unable to communicate with the DHCP server (`10.200.0.8`). The reachability test results are marked as \"unknown,\" indicating no response or incomplete testing.\\n     - Hosts are also unable to communicate with each other. The reachability test results between `host_1_1_1_1` and `host_2_1_1_1` are marked as \"unknown.\"\\n     - Hosts are unable to communicate with the DNS server, Load Balancer, and web servers. All tests involving these endpoints are marked as \"unknown.\"\\n\\n2. **Host-Specific Observations**:\\n   - Both `host_1_1_1_1` and `host_2_1_1_1` seem to be isolated from the rest of the network. This could indicate issues at the access layer (switches or access links) or problems with DHCP relay configuration.\\n\\n3. **Infrastructure Observations**:\\n   - The DHCP server, DNS server, Load Balancer, and web servers are interconnected and functioning correctly within the server farm subnet (`10.200.0.0/24`).\\n   - The OSPF routing between core and distribution routers may be functioning correctly for the server farm subnet, but there could be issues with routes to the host subnets (`10.<core>.<dist>.0/24`).\\n\\n#### **Potential Root Causes**\\n- **Access Layer Issues**:\\n  - The access switches (`switch_access_1_1_1` and `switch_access_2_1_1`) or their uplinks to the distribution routers may be misconfigured or experiencing failures.\\n  - Host interfaces or VLAN configurations may be incorrect, preventing communication with the DHCP server and other devices.\\n\\n- **Routing Problems**:\\n  - OSPF may not be advertising routes to the host subnets (`10.<core>.<dist>.0/24`) correctly, leading to reachability issues.\\n\\n- **DHCP Relay Misconfiguration**:\\n  - The DHCP relay configuration on the distribution routers may be incorrect, preventing hosts from obtaining IP addresses.\\n\\n#### **Next Steps**\\nFurther investigation is required to pinpoint the exact cause of the connectivity issues. This includes:\\n- Verifying the network configuration of the hosts and access switches.\\n- Checking OSPF configurations and routing tables on the routers.\\n- Inspecting DHCP relay settings on the distribution routers.\\n\\nThis concludes the diagnostic report., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='cfef48fa-d7c4-4f87-8643-90e8e2c300f8'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
